# The walk keeps every instance of a statement it reaches.
#
# The bound is 15 and not 12: three of the sixteen values written are
# never read, and the closure formulation dropped exactly those.  A
# sharpening that put the bound back to 12 would be unsound in general,
# so it is the bound that is pinned.
for \(int c0 = 0; c0 <= 15; c0 \+= 1\)
a\[c0\] = \(c0\);
if \(c0 <= 12\)
